    "faq_eyebrow": "Clarity before you begin",
    "faq_title": "A few useful answers.",
    "faq_0_q": "Can curtains work on angled windows?",
    "faq_0_a": "Yes, with a design suited to the shape, support and curtain weight. A sloping top does not always operate like a straight track: the specialist team agrees what moves and where fabric remains.",
    "faq_1_q": "Can I have blackout lining?",
    "faq_1_a": "Blackout lining can reduce light through the cloth. Overall darkness also depends on coverage, track position and gaps around the edges. These details need particular care in bedrooms.",
    "faq_2_q": "What should I send for an enquiry?",
    "faq_2_a": "A clear photograph of the whole window, your location and a short description are a useful start. Share approximate dimensions if you can measure safely. Final measurements and the fixing arrangement need specialist confirmation.",
    "faq_3_q": "How much do apex curtains cost?",
    "faq_3_a": "Each project is quoted around its shape, size, fabric, track and service requirements. Use the Apex Curtains enquiry link for a project quotation.",
    "faq_4_q": "Who provides measuring and fitting?",
    "faq_4_a": "Specialist surveys and installation are arranged through Apex Curtains, which currently advertises service across England and Wales. Confirm your location and access requirements with the team.",
    "faq_5_q": "Can Natalie give me a final quotation?",
    "faq_5_a": "Natalie is an AI adviser who can help you explore options and prepare questions. The Apex Curtains team confirms the final design, service and price. A chat is not a submitted project enquiry.",
